{"requirements":[{"id":"encrypted-volume","requirement":"Provide an encrypted volume on node1 mounted at /srv/secure.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A root-owned 256 MiB LUKS1 backing file was created, opened as /dev/mapper/securedata, formatted ext4, and mounted read/write at /srv/secure. The LUKS header, active encryption mapping, filesystem, mount source, and successful writes were directly observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60f065dedd874a97","cmd-e4f63bbb69574868","cmd-6fa3bc20b9694b49","cmd-7b5fa9dfb6c44b17"]},{"id":"automatic-boot-recovery","requirement":"The encrypted volume must unlock and mount automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"crypttab and fstab contain the required entries and systemd generated the corresponding cryptsetup unit. A bounded reboot changed the boot ID, after which the cryptsetup and mount units were active, /srv/secure was mounted from the encrypted mapping, pre-reboot data persisted, and the filesystem remained writable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f38a364b9b414d79","cmd-6d504900b91d438b","cmd-75e7c623bda343f5","cmd-74395ff40a0b4c8e","cmd-1ac029bc9b0a474f","cmd-7b5fa9dfb6c44b17","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creation and formatting of the encrypted volume, key, mount directory, and boot configuration were required implementation steps (cmd-60f065dedd874a97, cmd-e4f63bbb69574868, cmd-f38a364b9b414d79). Closing and reactivating the mapping, writing bounded test markers, rebooting, and performing a post-reboot write were directly tied to validating automatic recovery and persistence (cmd-6fa3bc20b9694b49, cmd-75e7c623bda343f5, cmd-7b5fa9dfb6c44b17). Final observations show no failed services, package damage, new listening sockets, or abnormal temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60f065dedd874a97","cmd-e4f63bbb69574868","cmd-f38a364b9b414d79","cmd-6fa3bc20b9694b49","cmd-75e7c623bda343f5","cmd-7b5fa9dfb6c44b17","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. Direct evidence establishes a working LUKS-encrypted ext4 volume at /srv/secure and demonstrates automatic unlock, mount, data persistence, and continued write access across a real reboot. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it includes a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service and data state.","limitations":[]}
